{"assets":["/statement-assets/a54fb351ab2de8992bc504129307a67bad3836b8ac39631ff328e59e4fd28647.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1726","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Jatayu's Balanced Bracket Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Last summer, Feluda gifted Lalmohan-Babu a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balanced"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" bracket sequence $$$s$$$ of length $$$2 n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Topshe was bored during his summer vacations, and hence he decided to draw an undirected graph of $$$2 n$$$ vertices using the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balanced bracket sequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$. For any two distinct vertices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\lt j \\le 2 n$$$), Topshe draws an edge (undirected and unweighted) between these two nodes if and only if the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsegment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s[i \\ldots j]$$$ forms a balanced bracket sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"connected components"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Topshe's graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"See the Notes section for definitions of the underlined terms."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of opening brackets in string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$2 n$$$ — a balanced bracket sequence consisting of $$$n$$$ opening brackets \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and $$$n$$$ closing brackets \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the number of connected components in Topshe's graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1\n()\n3\n()(())\n3\n((()))\n4\n(())(())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n2\n3\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sample explanation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the graph constructed from the bracket sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", is just a graph containing nodes $$$1$$$ and $$$2$$$ connected by a single edge. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the graph constructed from the bracket sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" would be the following (containing two connected components):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a54fb351ab2de8992bc504129307a67bad3836b8ac39631ff328e59e4fd28647.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Definition of Underlined Terms"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A sequence of brackets is called balanced if one can turn it into a valid math expression by adding characters $$$+$$$ and $$$1$$$. For example, sequences "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()(()))"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are balanced, while "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()))("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are not."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The subsegment $$$s[l \\ldots r]$$$ denotes the sequence $$$[s_l, s_{l + 1}, \\ldots, s_r]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A connected component is a set of vertices $$$X$$$ such that for every two vertices from this set there exists at least one path in the graph connecting these vertices, but adding any other vertex to $$$X$$$ violates this rule."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1726C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1726/problem/C"}